course: dictionary
lesson: 248
title: Alpaca: an animal and its wool
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can name a living thing and also something made from it. The clues around the word show you which meaning fits. In «Llamas and alpacas live in the Andes», the word live tells you that alpacas are animals.
explain: Alpaca has two meanings. The first is an animal: a South American animal like a small llama, with a long neck and very soft, thick wool. The second is the wool itself, which is used for jumpers, scarves and blankets.
explain: To check, swap in your meaning. In «A cow's stomach has four chambers, an alpaca's three», the stomach belongs to the animal, so alpaca means the animal. In «alpaca wool», the word alpaca tells you what kind of wool it is, so it names the material.
fact: Alpaca (the animal): a South American animal like a small llama, with a long neck and very soft, thick wool.
fact: Alpaca (the wool): the soft wool from this animal, used for jumpers, scarves and blankets.
fact: Alpacas come from the Andes mountains in Peru, Bolivia and Chile, where people have kept them for thousands of years for their wool.
fact: Alpacas are herbivores, so they eat plants, and they live in herds.
fact: Alpacas can spit when they are annoyed, but they spit more often at each other than at people.
exercise: «Llamas and alpacas live in the Andes.» What kind of thing is an alpaca? | A kind of potato | *An animal like a small llama | A type of jumper | A mountain in South America
exercise: «Alpaca wool» is used to make what? | Cars and bicycles | Roads for carrying loads | *Jumpers, scarves and blankets
exercise: Alpacas come from the Andes mountains. Which country is one of the places they come from? | *Peru | Egypt | France
test: «A cow's stomach has four chambers, an alpaca's three.» In this sentence, what does alpaca mean? | The soft wool used for jumpers | A blanket | A mountain in the Andes | *An animal
test: Which sentence uses alpaca to mean the wool? | The alpaca spat at the gate. | Three alpacas grazed on the hill. | *I knitted a scarf from alpaca.
exam: Alpacas are herbivores. What does herbivore mean? | *An animal that eats plants | An animal that eats meat | An animal that lives under water | A type of wool
